! An unconditional branch whose TARGET is index-modified.
!
! HOW THIS WAS FOUND.  mutation_score.py replaced
! "o.target = effAddr19(st, bm.addr, bm.idx)" with the raw address --
! dropping index modification of the branch target entirely -- and the
! mutation SURVIVED the whole suite.  effAddr19 returns the raw address
! unchanged when idx is 0, so a survivor means exactly one thing: not
! one program in the suite branches through an index register.  Over
! 160 programs, and the feature was completely unexercised.
!
! THE RULE, Reference Manual p.20-21 "Address Modification": the
! (signed) value field of the index register is added to the
! instruction's address field, and p.39 makes it apply to branching
! like anything else -- "any of these instruction types may cause a new
! value to be transferred to the instruction counter".
!
! UNITS ARE THE TRICK.  effAddr19 adds the index value's low 19 bits to
! a HALF-WORD address, and the value field is a BIT address, so a value
! of 1 moves the target by one half-word.  LVI cannot express that --
! it shifts its immediate left by five (see io_reader_printer.strap's
! own note) -- so the offset comes from an XW whose value field is the
! bit address (8)0.01, which is 1.
!
! WEAKER STANDARD, STATED: hand-written from p.20-21, not transcribed.

        SLC, (8)2740.0
!
! ---- case 1: a POSITIVE index value --------------------------------
START   LX, $1, WPLUS1               ! index value = +1 half-word
        B, T1($1)                    ! must land one half-word PAST T1
T1      BEW, $                       ! hang up: modification dropped
L1      B, C2                        ! T1 + 1: the correct landing
!
! ---- case 2: a NEGATIVE index value --------------------------------
! Case 1 alone does NOT pin the sign.  effAddr19 reads
! "(x.sign == 1) ? (raw - m) : (raw + m)", and a POSITIVE value takes
! the same branch whether or not the sign is honoured -- so case 1 dies
! only to a mutation that drops modification ENTIRELY, which is what it
! was originally written against.  An audit caught the claim that this
! program pinned the signed rule; it did not.  Only a negative value
! separates "raw - m" from "raw + m".
C2      LX, $1, WMINUS1              ! index value = -1 half-word
        B, T2($1)                    ! must land one half-word BEFORE T2
L2      B, PASS                      ! T2 - 1: the correct landing
T2      BEW, $                       ! hang up: modification dropped
        BEW, $                       ! hang up: the SIGN was ignored, so
                                     !   the branch ran the wrong way
WPLUS1  XW, (8)0.01, 0, 0, 0         ! value 1, sign 0
WMINUS1 XW, -(8)0.01, 0, 0, 0        ! value 1, sign 1
PASS    BEW, $
        END, START
